                <pb facs="0964" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg844"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">574.D 1/485</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Geddes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 414</seg></opener>
                <p>His Britannic Majesty’s Ambassador presents his compliments to the Secretary of
                    State and has the honour, on instructions from his Government, to inform him
                    that the following conclusions of the wireless experts on the subject of radio
                    communication in and with China have been approved by His Majesty’s Government:— <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>The conclusions agreed to by the American, British, French and
                            Japanese experts, and signed by Messrs. Walter S. Rogers, F. J. Brown,
                            M. Girardeau, K. Yoshino and Samosukie Inada on February 4th,
                            1922.</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>The Proposed Heads of Arrangement agreed to by the British, French and
                            Japanese experts, and signed by Messrs. F. J. Brown, M. Girardeau, K.
                            Yoshino and Samosukie Inada on the same date.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1922-06-02"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">June 2, 1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
